{"id": "EUVD-2026-97715", "enisaUuid": "13e5edee-d980-3116-8352-2484547ec009", "description": "ImageMagick 7.1.2-30 before 7.1.2-32 contains a use after free vulnerability in the WBINFO decoder that occurs when a memory allocation fails during image decoding. Attackers can supply a crafted image that, when decoded under memory allocation failure conditions, causes freed memory to be reused, crashing the application.", "datePublished": "2026-10-12T16:04:38", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-18T11:53:04", "baseScore": 6.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/security/advisories/GHSA-vxwm-jfjc-3r4x", "https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/commit/48c49d0cc2b72970b762e0d3263f6c35ab35a7b4", "https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/commit/2ed1b96b9bc71434f0c4e82e3c63fec029c684c6", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/imagemagick-7.1.2-30-before-7.1.2-32-use-after-free-in-wbinfo-decoder"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-109271", "GHSA-h82h-8q6v-f57g"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.37, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "a0b6abe5-3ab4-30d6-bcf7-e6941d5d25b7", "product": {"name": "ImageMagick", "vendor": {"name": "ImageMagick"}}, "product_version": "7.1.2-30 <7.1.2-32"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "ed3e4340-011c-3d60-a30e-1897b7452db4", "vendor": {"name": "ImageMagick"}}], "isExploited": false}